course: dictionary
lesson: 9088
title: One word, many meanings: slug
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. «At night the slugs come out, gliding on their slime and nibbling holes in the lettuce.» Slugs glide and eat lettuce, so here a slug is a small, soft animal.
explain: Slug can also mean a small amount of a drink swallowed quickly, or in slang a bullet, a fake coin, or a hard hit. To choose, look at the clues. A garden with lettuce means the animal. A cup of tea being gulped means the drink.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Dad had one slug of tea and ran for the bus.» If slug means a small amount of drink swallowed quickly, the sentence makes sense. That is how you know you have the right meaning.
fact: A slug is a small, soft animal with no shell and no legs.
fact: «A slug has four tentacles: the top two carry eyes and the bottom two feel and smell.»
fact: A slug glides on one wide, muscly foot and a trail of slime, which keeps it moist and helps it slide.
fact: Slugs come out at night and after rain, and they eat leaves and vegetables.
fact: «Slug pellets and rat poison can kill pets and wildlife», so wash your hands after touching slugs.
exercise: «At night the slugs come out, gliding on their slime and nibbling holes in the lettuce.» What is a slug in this sentence? | A small amount of drink swallowed quickly | *A small, soft animal with no shell | A fake coin | A bullet
exercise: Sam says, «Dad had one slug of tea and ran for the bus.» What does slug mean here? | A slow, slimy animal in the garden | A coin that is not real | To hit someone hard | *A small amount of a drink swallowed quickly
exercise: Slug pellets are poisonous to pets. What should you do after touching a slug? | Lick your fingers to taste it | Keep it in your pocket | *Wash your hands | Put it in your pet's bowl
test: What does the phrase «slow as a slug» tell you about a slug? | *It moves very slowly | It has four legs | It can fly | It moves very fast
test: Birds, hedgehogs and thrushes eat slugs. Why do gardeners sometimes dislike slugs? | Slugs sting people | Slugs make loud noises at night | Slugs have sharp tentacles | *Slugs nibble leaves and vegetables
exam: Read this: «The children stepped carefully over the slug trail on the path.» Which meaning of slug fits best? | *A small, soft animal with no shell | A fake coin | To hit someone hard | A small amount of a drink
